      "kind": "cohomology_window_and_relative_lifting",
      "original_statement": "A quasi-isomorphism induces an isomorphism on homotopy classes into a bounded-below injective complex; monomorphic quasi-isomorphisms allow strict lifts, unique up to homotopy.",
      "proved_statement": "For I^n=0 below a with injective terms, cohomology isomorphisms only in degrees n>=a suffice for the Hom comparison. A termwise monomorphism satisfying this range permits strict lifts, and two strict lifts have a homotopy vanishing on the original subcomplex. The explicit degree-reversing dual gives the projective version with n<=b and homotopies killed by the quotient map.",
      "hypotheses": "The actual target I, its lower term bound a and injective terms; the displayed cohomology range for the actual map. Strict statements additionally use its degreewise monomorphisms. Dual bounds and epimorphisms are explicitly proved.",
