      "kind": "both_prescribed_outer_resolutions",
      "original_statement": "A short exact sequence of bounded-below complexes has a compatible sequence of injective resolutions in which the first resolution may be prescribed.",
      "proved_statement": "Both outer injective resolutions may be prescribed, without requiring the given right-hand resolution map to be monic. A homotopy gives the upper-right entry h in the actual middle map [[1,h],[0,f_3]]. The explicitly computed projective dual retains both prescribed outer projective resolutions. Existing common term bounds are preserved.",
      "hypotheses": "The source short exact sequence and the two actually given bounded outer resolutions. No extra enough-injectives/projectives hypothesis is needed once those resolutions are supplied.",
